## Noncommercial Purposes

Any noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose.

Selling the software, or anything based on it, is never a
permitted purpose.  That includes offering it, or any part of
it, for a price, a fee or a subscription; with paid features,
unlocks or in-app purchases; with advertising built into it;
or as part of anything that is sold.

Two things are permitted purposes even where money is involved:

- asking for or accepting voluntary donations, tips or
  patronage for your own changes, new works or modules, as long
  as they are free to everyone and nothing in them is held back
  from anyone who does not pay; and

- playing the software and showing it, in videos, streams,
  screenshots, articles or reviews, even where those earn money.

## Personal Uses

Personal use for research, experiment, and testing for
