You may have "fair use" rights for the software under the
law. These terms do not limit them.

## The Original Game

The software plays Vampire: The Masquerade - Redemption, which
the licensor does not own and these terms do not provide.  To use
the software with it, you must own your own copy of it.

You may not distribute any of the original game's content (its
archives, levels, models, textures, sounds, music, movies,
scripts or any other of its files, or files converted from
them), other than what the licensor itself distributes with the
software, together with the software, with changes or new works
based on it, or with modules.  You may not use the software, or
anything based on it, to help anyone get the original game other
than by buying it from someone entitled to sell it.

## Where Vitomir Comes From

The licensor publishes the software, and the programs built from
its unchanged source, only in the official repository.  You may
not publish them anywhere else or offer them for download
anywhere else: link to the official repository instead.

You may publish the software's source code, changed or not, only
in a public fork of the official repository on GitHub.  A changed
version must carry a name other than Vitomir.

A module is a new work that runs on the software but contains
none of it.  You may publish a module anywhere, as long as it is
free to everyone, follows [The Original
Game](#the-original-game), and contains only your own work or
work whose owners have given you permission to share it.  Work
made by someone else, such as another person's mod, stays theirs
when it is made into a module or changed: publishing it needs
their permission.

## Names

The name Vitomir and its wordmark are the licensor's.  These
terms grant no rights in them.  A changed version must use
another name and must not present itself as Vitomir or as
official; it and a module may say truthfully that they run on
